gametitle=Grand Theft Auto: Vice City (NTSC-U Day 1 / CRC 20B19E49)
comment=Definitive Edition-style controls for Grand Theft Auto: Vice City.
comment=Built for the original PS2 default control scheme. Changing the in-game control type can produce different results.
comment=Enable group 1 for vehicle controls, group 2 for on-foot controls, and group 3 for native pause/menu input.
comment=Vehicle layout: L2 brake, R2 accelerate, L1 fire, R1 handbrake, Cross handbrake, Square look left, Circle look right, R3 look behind, D-pad Up vehicle sub-mission/misc, D-pad Right next station/radio.
comment=On-foot layout: L2 targeting, R2 attack, Circle attack, L1 next weapon, R1 camera reset, D-pad Left previous weapon, D-pad Right next weapon, and R3 native.
comment=The pause/menu guard restores native controls while a menu is open.
comment=Target: NTSC-U Day 1 SLUS-20552, CRC 20B19E49.
comment=Public credit: Zeroable.
comment=Control-remapping foundation based on PS2 Controller Remapper by pelvicthrustman.

[Cheats\1 REQUIRED - Definitive Edition vehicle controls]
description=Required vehicle controls. In vehicles: L2 brake, R2 accelerate, L1 fire, R1 or Cross handbrake, Square/Circle look left/right, R3 looks behind, D-pad Up activates the vehicle sub-mission or special action, and D-pad Right selects the next radio station. Native D-pad Left/Down are suppressed during gameplay. On-foot controls remain stock unless group 2 is enabled.
author=Zeroable

